<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Caucasus</p><h1 class="st-title">Terek Soviet Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1918 CE – 1918 CE · capital Pyatigorsk</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Soviet republic of 1918 in the Terek region, where Bolsheviks tried to govern Cossacks and mountain peoples amid civil war.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In March 1918 a congress of the peoples of the Terek region at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyatigorsk">Pyatigorsk</a> proclaimed the Terek Soviet Republic as part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-sfsr">Russian SFSR</a>. It covered the lands of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/terek-cossack-host">Terek Cossack Host</a> and of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chechens">Chechens</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ingush-people">Ingush</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ossetians">Ossetians</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabardians">Kabardians</a>, with its government at Pyatigorsk and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladikavkaz">Vladikavkaz</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The republic was led by a people's council and council of commissars under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samuil-buachidze">Samuil Buachidze</a> until his murder in June 1918. It tried to balance the claims of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossacks</a> and mountain peoples over land, while fighting the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mountainous-republic-of-the-northern-caucasus">Mountainous Republic of the Northern Caucasus</a> and anti-Bolshevik Cossacks. A Cossack uprising broke out in June 1918.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In July 1918 it was merged into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/north-caucasian-soviet-republic">North Caucasian Soviet Republic</a>, though its government survived in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladikavkaz">Vladikavkaz</a> until the White advance of early 1919. Soviet power returned in 1920, and the region was later divided into autonomous units for its peoples.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/terek-soviet-republic.jpg" alt="Terek Soviet Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: User:R-41 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Socialist_red_flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1918 CE – 1918 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Pyatigorsk</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Samuil Buachidze</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Russian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Terek SR</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=terek-soviet-republic" aria-label="Terek Soviet Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5712 618 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Terek Soviet Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6032 874L5820 533M6032 874L6032 874"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5820 533h0M6032 874h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6032 874h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6032 874h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Pyatigorsk. <a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=terek-soviet-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
